# Use `cn()` for Conditional Classes

Import `cn` from the project’s class-name utility when building dynamic or conditional `className` strings. Common locations are `@/lib/utils` (web) or `@/lib/utils/cn` (React Native / NativeWind). Never use backtick template literals with string interpolation for classes. Applies to any React component that accepts `className` (DOM elements, Radix/shadcn wrappers, NativeWind components, etc.).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — template literal interpolation
<div className={`flex-1 ${isActive ? 'bg-primary' : 'bg-muted'}`} />

// ❌ BAD — ternary inside template
<span className={`text-base ${disabled && 'opacity-50'}`} />

// ✅ GOOD — cn() merges and deduplicates classes correctly
<div className={cn('flex-1', isActive ? 'bg-primary' : 'bg-muted')} />

// ✅ GOOD — falsy values are safely ignored
<span className={cn('text-base', disabled && 'opacity-50')} />
```
